 "note": "Busselton Visitor Centre (Railway House), Foreshore Parade by the jetty, from docs/landmarks/visitor_centre.md (Landgate aerial, OSM outline, 2021 street photos). The 1894 station (white weatherboard, gable end with its brick chimney facing east), the new visitor centre joined to it (white boards, verandah with a dark fascia, louvred plant screen on the roof), the long low-pitched hall and train shed behind with solar panels. The front is the east face, the one seen square-on driving west along Foreshore Parade. Signs are plain lettering. Metres: x left to right as seen from the east (south to north), y back from the east face (westward).",
